WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.270
but before we go to this topic,
which is our main topic,

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:07.840
professor frankl, a question: we spoke
of collective guilt or of the

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.429
idea of collective guilt. it is debatable wether or not it truly exists, but

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:15.740
in any case, there was something and there is something we also gather from certain

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:21.300
reactions: there was collective
repression of this guilt.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.080
do you believe that now the time has come
and that this television show can contribute

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:31.560
to overcome this repression? yes but I
must say, paradoxically, only

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:38.280
and especially by our standing up
against the concept of collective guilt.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:47.670
you see, mr. kreuzer, i traveled 25 
times to america for

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:55.710
courses or to teach at universities. and always at the end students who

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:01.129
read the book you mentioned, come up to me

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:10.680
and say: mr. frankl, tell us
not just about your experiences in

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.020
psychotherapy but in the final
lecture, please tell us about

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.240
your experiences in the concentration camp.
and i am already prepared for that and

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.470
always bring a box with a few slides with me

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:29.930
which i took at the
former concentration camp of auschwitz,

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:35.460
when i visited many years ago
with two american guest professors

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:41.159
to show them and
explain certain things. so i show

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:50.340
them, for example, the half-bombed
gas chambers. i show them the ramp of

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.950
the train station where the first
"selection" took place and i had to walk

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:01.500
up to doctor mengele
who pointed with his finger

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.060
right or left - which meant to be or
not be. of our particular transport only

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:13.600
ten percent went to the right side. and
then i show them the barracks in

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:20.099
birkenau, you know, the
former horse stables. into each of these

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:26.660
stables they had crammed 1100 of us.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:32.390
and after showing them all these slides
i show them one last one

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:40.650
of a a farmhouse, located just about in the middle

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:47.040
between bad wörishofen and türkheim. 
türkheim was the last camp from which

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:54.060
i was liberated by troops from texas. and in front of
this farmhouse are a few farmers,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.860
their children, grandchildren .. three
generations. and then I say

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:05.459
to the students: now
look. these are the farmers, who

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:12.079
risked their lives by hiding
two jewish boys

00:03:12.079 --> 00:03:18.060
of our concentration camp from the ss.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.220
I always conclude with that, so that the
concept of collective guilt doesn't arise.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.819
the show actually speaks to that,

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:30.709
the wife who follows her jewish husband into the camp.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:35.819
exactly. mr. kreuzer, it confronts everyone with reality, albeit in an

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:40.980
artistically elevated way. and it gives to the person who is not guilty

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:46.380
an opportunity to
dissociate from the guilt. and it also gives

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:50.130
and opportunity to the one who is guilty:

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:54.359
the opportunity to distance himself from himself
and to grow.

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:58.489
in connection with the
overcoming of repression

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:03.450
the german psychologist mitscherlich
talks about "grief work", meaning

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:10.410
work that has to be done to
finally really mourn. is that

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:14.939
what this show does? i personally do not believe in that because all

00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:19.440
these concepts are far too psychodynamically oriented and see the human being

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.669
as a bunch of certain
psychological mechanisms and

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:30.419
thereby in a way give him an alibi.
this is about the human core and it

00:04:30.419 --> 00:04:34.120
is about personal guilt or
innocence. and there is only personal guilt.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.720
I think I am the only jew in this group

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.650
and maybe I have the
right or even the duty to

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:46.200
emphasize: there is only personal guilt
and no collective guilt. and if we

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.729
commit the mistake - or the
youth, which was far from it time wise

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:54.780
and not just internally, if we
leave our youth in the belief that

00:04:54.780 --> 00:05:00.270
there is collectively guilt, then we cause
the repression and

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:05.060
repressive tendencies.
we have to tell the young person:

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:11.010
if you blame the germans or the austrians collectively

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:17.039
you are doing exactly the same thing, the Nazis, especially the Nazis, did to the jews.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:21.650
we need to tell people that, 
while of course there are differences,

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:27.419
quantitative and certain
differences in style, the organizational,

00:05:27.419 --> 00:05:30.719
the technological and so on ...
we still have to tell the people

00:05:30.719 --> 00:05:37.560
that one hand should not pride itself

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:43.140
that it was the the other hand which was

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.530
affected by a disease and not itself.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:52.289
it is always the
whole organism that was sick

00:05:52.289 --> 00:05:57.320
the whole of humankind. and every single person,
I personally believe, is in principle

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:03.150
if not in the past so in the
future, capable of holocaust, vulnerable to

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:08.700
holocaust. holocaust is in each of us
designed as a human possibility,

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.570
or rather, 
as the inhumanity as possibility in a human being.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.360
this is perhaps our most important topic
anyway, but we want to come back

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.780
to that later. may i ask one last question about the topic,

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:22.830
overcoming repression - your colleague
ringel writes in this context:

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:26.670
it is important that this is not a documentary but something

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:30.840
experiential. because only the
emotional shock, the deep

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.860
consternation that this show
has caused is capable

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:38.910
to overcome the barrier in people,
to overcome repression. is that not

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:43.170
what makes this special and the reason why things are starting to move all in german speaking countries,

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.140
a willingness to think about all this?

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:50.430
of course the consternation of the audience which is so much talked about nowadays

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:55.260
can only emanate from something concrete and personal.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:07:00.060
but I do not want to
use the word "emotionality" because

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.500
I would infer something merely sentimental. it is more, it

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:10.080
is about something existential. it
is a confession, as you mr. president

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:15.210
indicated, it is a confession that must set the path for the future and

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:20.200
therefore should be a concern of education.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:27.080
pease, before we enter the historic core of thematter, 
i ask to show the three inserts.

